module test.claim.extdeps_scope_placement_gate_live_wet_witness

// THE EXECUTING ROUTE OF gunbc.instruments.extdeps_scope_placement_gate (roadmap node
// dp-m3-extdeps-scope-halved, gunbc#15583). Before this module the gate had THREE modeled
// enrollments and ZERO routes: a CommitSpecGate row in gunbc.commit_workflow::commit_gate_roster, a
// dispatch arm in gunbc.instruments.ci_gates::run_spec_gate whose main() nothing invokes, and
// extdeps_scope_placement_gate_passes in gunbc.instruments.floor_effect_gate_witness — a module with
// no test-marked decl, so floor discovery (which enrolls test-marked decls only) never planned it.
// The gate's own header asserted "fleet-executed (wet)" as of 2026-10-01; this module is what makes
// that sentence true by execution rather than by narration.
//
// WHAT THIS MODULE IS: the gate, run. Its one claim calls the gate's own entry
// (gunbc.instruments.extdeps_scope_placement_gate::run_extdeps_scope_placement_gate) and reports its
// ProcessExit. It re-implements no arm, re-reads no diff and decides nothing of its own: the gate
// stays the single authority over its four arms (membership over the merge base, freeze over the
// frozen anchor, language-module homing, manifest remove-only), and this module's only judgment is
// ExitSuccess or not. A red here is the gate's own located reason — arm named, offending path named —
// because the reason is built inside the gate and this claim only reports it.
//
// WHY WET, AND WHY THIS LANE: every live arm reads the PREPARED SUBJECT's git history —
// origin/main...HEAD for the placement and remove-only arms, legacy_manifest_freeze_sha..HEAD for the
// freeze arm. Hermetic admission needs a published mock_response per operation, and the placement
// arm's base is a MOVING ref, so no recorded SHA pair can serve it: that is exactly why
// test.claim.external_model_scope_witness is admitted hermetically (its base is the frozen anchor)
// while this gate cannot be. The module therefore declares ReadsLiveTree — the hermetic floor
// declines its identities BEFORE execution rather than pretending to serve them — and the identity is
// scheduled on the local-repo wet lane (v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal::local_repo_wet_schedule),
// which the required floor runner executes itself with real effects
// (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/required_floor_runner.rs). The lane's membership property is effects
// confined to a temporary directory and a local git repository: this claim reads git in the checkout
// and reads the frozen manifest file, nothing else.
//
// THE MUTATION CONTROLS OF THIS GATE ARE NOT HERE: they are supplied-observation verdicts with no git
// and no disk, and they live hermetically in test.claim.extdeps_scope_placement_gate_verdict_witness,
// where the floor can plan them every run for the cost of a resolution. Putting them here would have
// made a free control cost a wet slot and a git read. The quarantined pair in
// test.claim.long.extdeps_scope_placement_gate_loudness_witness stays where #8457 put it and is not
// duplicated: that pair probes the seed runner's failure-receipt channel, this route executes the
// verdict.

import extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io
import std.live_tree { LiveTreeDisposition, ReadsLiveTree }
import std.process { ExitSuccess }
import std.types { Bool }
import gunbc.instruments.extdeps_scope_placement_gate { run_extdeps_scope_placement_gate }

data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = ReadsLiveTree

// THE ENROLMENT CLAIM: the gate as authored, over the prepared subject, on the floor's own wet lane.

test fn the_placement_gate_verdict_passes_on_the_prepared_subject() -> Bool {
  match run_extdeps_scope_placement_gate() {
    ExitSuccess => true
    _ => false
  }
}
